SIDERATLAS — collection licensing

This repository is a collection of independently licensed components. There is
no single license grant for every file, dataset and rendered movie.

001-black-hole: the selected original release declares no general code or
media license. Publication here grants no additional reuse permission. See
its THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md for font terms.

002-pulsar: project software is GPL-2.0; see episodes/002-pulsar/LICENSE and
NOTICE. COFFEE and its dependencies retain their upstream notices. Its media
and caption remain all rights reserved. The GPL component is independent;
its code is not incorporated into the MIT episode implementations.

003-white-dwarf: original code is MIT, with separate GYRE GPLv3/WDEC notices
for supplied equilibrium inputs and separate data/font terms. See the episode
LICENSE, licenses/ and METHODS.md. Raw atmosphere tables remain external; selected calculated integrations and
fixed-model optical inputs are supplied with attribution. This collection
grants no new rights to the providers’ raw atmosphere libraries.

004-main-sequence-star, 005-stellar-merger, 006-planetary-nebula,
007-spiral-galaxy:
original code/documentation and author-generated numerical outputs retain
their episode MIT notices. This does not license external datasets, fonts or
rendered media. Dataset attribution and redistribution restrictions remain
in the episode documentation and manifests.

shared/video_export.py: unchanged No.004 encoder, MIT; see shared/LICENSE.
shared/fonts/: unmodified Latin Modern GUST/LPPL fonts and STIX Two Math OFL;
all original notices and source inventories are retained beside the fonts.
CIE 1931 CSV/metadata: unmodified CC BY-SA 4.0 data, separately attributed in
the episode methods. No permission for data is inferred from a software license.

Original movies, thumbnails and captions retain their previously stated
media rights. No new blanket media license is granted. Paper citations do
not authorize redistribution or imply endorsement. No paper PDFs, NASA footage,
raw Bifrost cubes, compiler binaries or private requested datasets are bundled.
